<%#
  Said plainly. The link is dead by the time this renders, so there is nothing
  here to undo — and nothing about the account has changed, which is the point:
  ending the reminders on this device is not the same as ending the arrangement,
  and only the first is something a web address should be able to do.
%>
<div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
  <div class="text-center">
    <p class="text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8">Reminders stopped</p>

    <p class="text-3xl text-gray-700 mb-4">
      This device will not show or speak your reminders any more.
    </p>

    <p class="text-2xl text-gray-600">
      If you change your mind, ask the person who set this up to send you a new link.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
